How to interpret the result
If this returns 200

Then Auth0 config is probably okay, and your interceptor Lambda likely has a network/VPC problem.

Then check:

is the interceptor Lambda attached to a VPC?

if yes, does it have outbound internet access via NAT?

can it resolve external DNS?

If this returns 4xx

Then the request reached Auth0, but Auth0 rejected it. That means we need to inspect:

audience

scope

app permissions

whether token exchange is enabled for that app/API

If this also throws a connection error

Then your domain/value is wrong or there’s a broader connectivity issue.

Also check one easy thing right now

Make sure:

AUTH0_DOMAIN = dev-xxxxx.us.auth0.com

and not:

AUTH0_DOMAIN = https://dev-xxxxx.us.auth0.com

Because your code already does:

f"https://{AUTH0_DOMAIN}/oauth/token"

If you included https:// in the env var, the URL becomes malformed.

